# Transforms: always Zod

All transforms from raw/external data (PocketBase records, HTTP JSON, scraper payloads, etc.) into app/domain shapes must go through a **Zod schema**. Do not hand-roll `typeof` / field-copy mappers.

## Patterns

- Define a schema (`z.object`, …) next to the type; export `type X = z.infer<typeof xSchema>`.
- Prefer `safeParse` (or a small `parseX` helper) over throwing `parse` in services.
- Put shared client+server shapes in `#lib/...` (not under `server/`). Server-only transforms stay under `#lib/server`.
- Services own the transform call and return `Result` / `ResultAsync` (neverthrow) — load functions and remotes call the service, they do not re-implement mapping.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — schema + parse helper
import { z } from 'zod';

export const appUserSchema = z.object({
	id: z.string().min(1),
	email: z.string().default(''),
	name: z
		.string()
		.nullish()
		.transform((value) => value ?? null)
});

export type AppUser = z.infer<typeof appUserSchema>;

export function parseAppUser(raw: unknown): AppUser | null {
	const result = appUserSchema.safeParse(raw);
	return result.success ? result.data : null;
}
```

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — service uses the schema
import type { AppError } from '#lib/server/result.js';
import { ERROR_CODE, panic } from '#lib/server/result.js';

currentUser(): Result<AppUser | null, AppError> {
	const record = this.ctx.locals.user;
	if (!record) {
		return ok(null);
	}

	const user = parseAppUser(record);
	if (!user) {
		return panic(ERROR_CODE.AUTH_INVALID_USER, 500, 'Invalid authenticated user record');
	}

	return ok(user);
}
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — manual typeof mapper
function toAppUser(record: RecordModel): AppUser {
	return {
		id: record.id,
		email: typeof record.email === 'string' ? record.email : '',
		name: typeof record.name === 'string' ? record.name : null
	};
}
```

## Do not

- Copy fields with ad-hoc `typeof` / `in` checks when Zod can describe the shape
- Transform in `+layout.server` / `+page.server` / remotes when a service method should own it
- Duplicate the same mapper in client and server modules
- Use Valibot or another schema library — prefer Zod
